        <item>
            <key> <string>description</string> </key>
            <value> <string encoding="cdata"><![CDATA[

Read a single ERP5 document with full field details, workflows, and metadata.\n
\n
    Returns field values with editability info, available workflow actions,\n
    views/tabs, listbox metadata, download/print actions, and jump links.\n
\n
    USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - You need full details of ONE document (all fields, types, editability).\n
    - You need to check which fields are editable before calling erp5_write.\n
    - You need to discover workflow actions before calling erp5_action.\n
    - You need to find available views, download/print actions, or sub-object types.\n
    - You need MatrixBox data (specify the view, e.g. view=\'quantity_view\').\n
    - You need editable fields from ALL views at once - set all_editable=true.\n
\n
    DO NOT USE THIS WHEN:\n
    - You need a full document tree with children - use erp5_read_deep instead.\n
    - You need all rows from a listbox - use erp5_collect after reading.\n
    - You want to search for documents - use erp5_search.\n
\n
    TYPICAL FLOWS:\n
    - Edit: erp5_read (check editable fields) -> erp5_write.\n
    - Workflow: erp5_read (check available actions) -> erp5_action.\n
    - Listbox: erp5_read (get listbox metadata) -> erp5_collect (get all rows).\n
\n
    - Report: erp5_read on the module -> the \'reports\' array -> erp5_collect with\n
      that name as \'view\' for the rows, or erp5_download with it as action_name\n
      for a file. erp5_read on the report action itself shows the dialog: its\n
      parameters, and under \'dialog.renders\' the form that actually holds the\n
      rows. all_listboxes is null on a dialog - normal, and not a sign that there\n
      is nothing to collect.\n


]]></string> </value>
